{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A three-dimensional rectangular box with dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> has faces whose surface areas are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> square units. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec42889bab8f60120619349190d29140f61861ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }18 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }22 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }24 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }30 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }36 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the length of the shortest dimension and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be the length of the longest dimension. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f4862f5341ba4081911b57c5ffcbd77588b1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c6dc668d3fd6954f1cd5d0d8d8c44646f79e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ = 72$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8acce8bf8459bc5cb2457c1cc16ae0ded938b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XZ = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />.\nDivide the first two equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/453bd7729aff206958577eaf5f21110f7d50046d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Z}{X} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />. Then, multiply by the last equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a3084676741076a80840a27f1eacbe16499929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/9901435fd585237103f96ac7445953c182652d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />. Following, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b3019aa161a29f20e67e2a7660f20d82c8d2573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84064a370f909fee73ba528860c52f5ac99d35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = 6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/607c6992d0667577abf471ae03ce28edfef62c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 6 + 12 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Simply guess and check to find that the dimensions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/7/607c6992d0667577abf471ae03ce28edfef62c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 6 + 12 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\nWhile this can definitely work it is not guaranteed and is not advised.\n~minor edit Washingtonsee\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you find the GCD of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94db15b430439ad5b3c80bfacfef0c6499ede2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> you get your first number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. After this, do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/447be73ee4469b54f92d15c8506f4bdba3d265f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48 \\div 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/62926bd52a6780574985021148fd0cd4d989fb6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72 \\div 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the other 2 numbers. When you add up your <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the surface areas of the faces are the product of two of the dimensions. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c9a2f4b4ca90475fc5a19e6ddcafb9733ead333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c7437ae6dcdf5f365311618ebd97ceefeb6759f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XZ=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d13ef41d7d3e1f3d76588326dfd0a0305229b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ=72$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />. You can multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84df6afd9a741fcb76bd1b60d35bf9468fd8916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY \\times XZ \\times YZ$\" width=\"134\" height=\"12\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/1082a2c6a2e98d7e8e741b92a5a09fa9f5ff4f19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${XYZ}^2=24 \\times 48 \\times 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" /> which means that the volume<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> equals<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee4ac821ec9c1d956ca0ae079a438d963f86f97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{24*48*72}=\\sqrt{24^2*12^2}=24*12=288$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"340\" height=\"19\" />. The individual dimensions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> can be found by doing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f0537130ba6c176b4896a31c0a5dabba042f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XYZ}{XY}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b26ee311b3c1e627cf865bafef5f1dc9fea268c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XYZ}{YZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6f18dd53b471691519ade8718f6d6531dbab21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{XYZ}{XZ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69ec3c81db87b4cbb4f2b07cc29e50d0ca8b2f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d614c4fb0f73528942bace8926fbe646803f36dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y=6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/14425c57745d2c13c539e983550d2ef419b78242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />. Adding this up, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43824492bdedb709c08da6583b6ad8276df7472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X+Y+Z=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n- Solution by smartninja2000\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FFrcsd9TzdM\">https://youtu.be/FFrcsd9TzdM</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/iIgNr9XUneg\">https://youtu.be/iIgNr9XUneg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B\">2018 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a 